<Window x:Class="RxVerifyOverlay.Integrated.ReportErrorWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Title="Report an error — Rx Verify"
        Width="420" SizeToContent="Height"
        MinWidth="360"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterScreen"
        ResizeMode="NoResize"
        ShowInTaskbar="True"
        Topmost="True">
    <!--
        "Report error…" dialog (verdict-tooltips-reports branch) — opened
        from a verdict bar's right-click context menu
        (Integrated/IntegratedBoxesWindow.cs ReportErrorRequested ->
        Integrated/IntegratedOverlayCoordinator.cs -> MainWindow.xaml.cs).
        UNLIKE IntegratedBoxesWindow/ControlBoxWindow, this is a NORMAL
        (activatable, non-click-through) window — it needs real keyboard
        focus for the correction TextBox. Owner is deliberately NOT set to
        MainWindow (see MainWindow.xaml.cs OpenReportErrorDialog's doc):
        MainWindow can be hidden in Integrated display mode, and a
        ShowDialog against a hidden owner is unreliable — WindowStartupLocation
        ="CenterScreen" instead of "CenterOwner" is what makes that safe.

        Prefilled fields (Field/Status/Source/Entered) are READ-ONLY plain
        text, never editable — the pharmacist's only input is the
        Correction TextBox. Source/Entered here are shown verbatim for a
        normal field. 2026-08-18 ("right-click must work on EVERY field"):
        this dialog now DOES open for the 3 patient-identity fields too
        (patientName/patientDOB/patientAddress) — see
        IntegratedBoxesWindow.PollCursorForHover, which used to never raise
        ReportErrorRequested for them at all. For those fields, code-behind
        swaps Source/Entered for a "[hidden — patient field]" placeholder
        on screen — Reporting/RxReportBuilder.cs still redacts both
        defensively before anything is ever sent, belt-and-suspenders, so
        even a future on-screen regression here can't leak PHI into the
        payload.

        2026-08-19 policy change (Will verbatim: "it won't let me type
        anything in the box... Fix that"): CorrectionTextBox is now ENABLED
        for patient fields too (it used to be disabled outright, which was
        this exact bug) — PatientFieldNoteText warns against typing the
        patient's actual data instead, and RxReportBuilder.Build's
        PatientFieldCorrectionGuard is the actual enforcement: it withholds
        the typed text (replacing it with a fixed stand-in, same as before
        this change) ONLY if it detects the patient's real captured value
        leaking into it — otherwise the typed description is sent as-is.
        CorrectionGuardNoteText is live, on-screen-only feedback for that
        same check, re-run on every keystroke; see code-behind's
        OnCorrectionTextChanged.

        RXVERIFY-TROUBLESHOOT ROUND 2 (2026-08, owner: "Alt+Tab shows NO
        Report error window anywhere — the dialog NEVER opens"):
        ShowInTaskbar was previously "False". WPF's ShowInTaskbar="False"
        sets WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW under the hood, and Windows excludes an
        UN-OWNED WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW window from Alt-Tab — so Will's own
        diagnostic (Alt+Tab) could never have told "the dialog never
        opened" apart from "the dialog opened but is invisible to
        Alt-Tab by its own styling", which would make the round-1
        Activate()/Topmost fix in MainWindow.xaml.cs look like it failed
        even if it actually worked. Flipped to "True" so this dialog is
        always genuinely findable (taskbar AND Alt-Tab) regardless of
        where the real bug turns out to be — see MainWindow.xaml.cs
        OpenReportErrorDialog's own doc for the rest of round 2's
        instrumentation.
    -->
    <Grid Margin="14">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <TextBlock x:Name="FieldNameText" Grid.Row="0" Text="Field" FontSize="16" FontWeight="Bold" Margin="0,0,0,8" />

        <Border Grid.Row="1" Background="#FFF3F3F3" BorderBrush="#FFD5D5D5" BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="3" Padding="8" Margin="0,0,0,10">
            <StackPanel>
                <TextBlock x:Name="StatusText" Text="Status: " TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,4" />
                <TextBlock x:Name="SourceText" Text="Source: " TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,4" />
                <TextBlock x:Name="EnteredText" Text="Entered: " TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,4" />
                <TextBlock x:Name="ExplanationText" Text="" TextWrapping="Wrap" FontStyle="Italic" Foreground="#FF555555" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Border>

        <!--
            2026-08-19 policy change (Will verbatim: "it won't let me type
            anything in the box... Fix that"): shown only for the 3
            patient-identity fields (VerdictFieldInfo.IsPatientField) — see
            code-behind's constructor. The Correction box below is now
            ENABLED for these fields too (it used to be disabled entirely,
            which is the bug this note replaces the explanation for) — this
            warns the pharmacist to describe the PROBLEM, not restate the
            patient's actual data, since Reporting/RxReportBuilder.cs still
            enforces that as a hard rule (see PatientFieldCorrectionGuard)
            regardless of what this note says.
        -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="PatientFieldNoteText" Grid.Row="2"
                   Text="Patient field — describe the problem WITHOUT typing the patient's actual name/DOB/address. This report leaves this computer."
                   TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="11" FontStyle="Italic" Foreground="#FF8A6D00" Margin="0,0,0,6"
                   Visibility="Collapsed" />

        <TextBlock x:Name="CorrectionPromptText" Grid.Row="3" Text="What's wrong / what should this have been?" Margin="0,0,0,4" />
        <TextBox x:Name="CorrectionTextBox" Grid.Row="4" AcceptsReturn="True" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                 Height="80" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" Margin="0,0,0,4" />

        <!--
            2026-08-19: live feedback only — see code-behind's
            OnCorrectionTextChanged, wired for patient fields only.
            PatientFieldCorrectionGuard re-runs on every keystroke purely
            to show/hide this; the actual send-time decision is always
            re-computed authoritatively inside Reporting/RxReportPayload.cs
            RxReportBuilder.Build, never trusted from this UI-only check.
        -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="CorrectionGuardNoteText" Grid.Row="5"
                   Text="Your note appears to contain the patient's actual info — it was kept on this PC; describe the pattern instead."
                   TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="11" FontStyle="Italic" Foreground="#FFB00020" Margin="0,0,0,10"
                   Visibility="Collapsed" />

        <!--
            2026-08-18: shown only when OverlaySettings.RxVerifyReportKey
            is unset on this workstation (ReportErrorRequestInfo.ReportingEnabled
            == false) — right-click used to be silently swallowed entirely
            in this case (RightClickOutcomeClassifier's old
            SuppressedReportingDisabled). Now the dialog always opens; this
            note plus SubmitButton.IsEnabled = false (see code-behind) make
            the reason visible instead of a click that just does nothing.
        -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="NotSetUpNoteText" Grid.Row="6"
                   Text="Error reporting isn't set up on this PC — re-run the pinned setup line from HQ."
                   TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="11" FontWeight="Bold" Foreground="#FFB00020" Margin="0,0,0,10"
                   Visibility="Collapsed" />

        <StackPanel Grid.Row="7" Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Right">
            <Button x:Name="CancelButton" Content="Cancel" Padding="12,4" Margin="0,0,8,0" Click="OnCancelClick" IsCancel="True" />
            <Button x:Name="SubmitButton" Content="Submit" Padding="12,4" Click="OnSubmitClick" IsDefault="True" />
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</Window>
